{
  "_comment": "Hosting/CDN ASN registry: ASN -> generic provider facts. Read by wp_ippivot to decide whether a shared IP is an operator signal or shared-tenancy noise, and to route abuse contact. GROWS AUTOMATICALLY \u2014 wp_ippivot.asn_registry_upsert banks each new ASN it meets, so hand-editing is only needed to correct a `noise` or `kind` call. See _meta for the field contract and the RULE 1 opsec constraint.",
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Known hosting/CDN ASNs -> GENERIC provider facts, used by wp_ippivot to decide whether an IP is same-operator signal or shared noise, and to route abuse/takedown contact.",
    "opsec": "Provider-level metadata ONLY (ASN, org name, abuse contact, noise flag, kind). NEVER a target IP, domain, or case id (repo CLAUDE.md RULE 1). wp_ippivot.asn_registry_upsert enforces this.",
    "fields": "asns[ASxxxx] = {asn, name, abuse_contacts[], noise(bool), kind: cdn|cloud|hosting|transit|unknown}",
    "noise": "noise=true means a reverse-IP on this ASN returns many unrelated tenants -> mark the IP as INFORMATION, do not cluster on it."
